  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Business And Technical Evaluation Checklist",
      "anchor": "business-and-technical-evaluation-checklist"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Use this checklist before selecting Nodics for a product or customer program. Record evidence, owners, risks, and follow-up actions rather than answering only yes or no."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Business Fit",
      "anchor": "business-fit"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "What business capability will the first release prove?",
        "How many customer or tenant variations are expected?",
        "Which foundations would otherwise need to be designed and maintained by the"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "delivery team?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "What is the expected product lifetime and team growth?",
        "Does the organization accept a governed framework in exchange for less"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "architectural freedom?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "What delivery-time and maintenance-cost measures will be compared?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Product And Delivery Fit",
      "anchor": "product-and-delivery-fit"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Build one representative capability, not only a hello-world route.",
        "Demonstrate API, data, permissions, configuration, tests, and documentation.",
        "Demonstrate a project-level customization without editing framework source.",
        "Identify which available modules are production-ready and which require"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "further implementation or provider qualification."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Estimate team learning, migration, and operational enablement effort."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Security And Compliance Fit",
      "anchor": "security-and-compliance-fit"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Read [Why Businesses Can Trust Nodics](/docs/business/security-and-trust), assign the"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[Security Shared-Responsibility Model](/docs/security/shared-responsibility-model), and validate claims with the [Security Evidence Guide](/docs/security/security-evidence-guide)."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Verify human authentication separately from module-to-module and scheduled"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "access."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Verify authorization, tenant isolation, validation, secrets handling, audit,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "and sensitive-data treatment."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Confirm regulatory, retention, residency, encryption, and evidence needs for"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "the intended deployment."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Test failure and misuse cases, not only successful access.",
        "Record which controls are framework-provided, project-configured,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "infrastructure-operated, and organization-owned."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Do not accept certification or compliance claims without solution-specific"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "evidence and the required independent assessment."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Architecture And Integration Fit",
      "anchor": "architecture-and-integration-fit"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Confirm which module owns every proposed capability.",
        "Identify external systems, data contracts, failure behavior, retries, and"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "provider ownership."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Check for existing Nodics capabilities before introducing a second loader,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "registry, policy engine, or source of truth."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Confirm how frontend applications consume APIs while Nodics remains the"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "backend/API platform."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Define the path from the initial topology to expected scale."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Operations And Commercial Fit",
      "anchor": "operations-and-commercial-fit"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Define service-level objectives, observability, incident response, backup,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "recovery, and capacity expectations."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Verify deployment automation and environment separation.",
        "Determine internal ownership, support expectations, licensing obligations,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "and upgrade responsibility."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Estimate the total cost of the complete solution, including infrastructure,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "providers, delivery, operation, and training."
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Decision Record",
      "anchor": "decision-record"
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The final decision should state:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "the business outcomes Nodics is expected to improve;",
        "proof-of-concept evidence;",
        "known gaps and required investments;",
        "selected providers and their maturity;",
        "security and operational acceptance;",
        "accountable business and technical owners;",
        "exit or reassessment criteria."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Continue",
      "anchor": "continue"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unordered-list",
      "items": [
        "Previous: [How Nodics Compares](/docs/business/how-nodics-compares)",
